  "question": {
    "text": "Two capacitors of capacitances <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;are charged to potential differences <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></math>, respectively. These are then connected in parallel in such a manner that the positive terminal of one is connected to the negative terminal of the other. The final energy of this configuration is :"
  },
